Exclude every node_modules from the image build context

The control-plane build never reached Azure. It sat packing the context
and was killed twice before I measured what it was packing: 420 MB of
node_modules under workload/, which arrived long after .dockerignore was
written and which nothing in the root-context images uses.

The file already carried a warning about a 1 GiB sparse .dat turning a
twenty-second build into a very long one. The same trap, a different
directory, and the entry that would have caught it was scoped to the one
node_modules that existed at the time.

Now excluded globally, along with workload/ itself: neither the control
plane nor the sidecar copies anything from it, and the CDC gateway
builds from its own directory as its own context, so this file does not
apply to it.

The build now completes in 1m33s.

Also records in SAAS.md what baking the site into the control-plane image
costs. It buys a real property - the download page cannot advertise a
build the fleet is not running, because both leave in one image - but it
is paid for in editorial friction, and friction of that shape stops
small corrections being made. Three false claims on the site were found
this evening. Decoupling the static site while keeping /downloads/ in
the image is noted as planned.

